I removed the `as` casts from the new `setValidationMany` code in `KoBoToolbox.node.ts`. Nothing I added still uses `as`. The remaining hits are in existing code, which I left alone.

The change replaces the two casted reads with typed reads and a type guard:

```ts
const rawSubmissionIds = this.getNodeParameter('submissionIds', i);
const status = this.getNodeParameter('validationStatus', i);
if (typeof rawSubmissionIds !== 'string' || typeof status !== 'string') {
	throw new NodeOperationError(
		this.getNode(),
		'Submission IDs and validation status must be text',
		{ itemIndex: i },
	);
}
const submissionIds = parseCommaSeparatedList(rawSubmissionIds);
```

The guard narrows both values to `string`, so the rest of the block is unchanged. Tests, lint, and the app were not run, as you asked.
